From: =?UTF-8?q?Juan=20Manuel=20L=C3=B3pez=20Carrillo?=
 <juanmanuellopezcarrillo@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 23 Jun 2026 12:57:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 004/143] dts: opi4a: reserve the secure firmware regions as
 no-map

The vendor U-Boot reserves BL31, OP-TEE and the shared-memory regions in
the FDT it hands to its own kernel, but not in the mainline DTB. Without
those reservations the kernel used the memory as ordinary RAM and
overwrote BL31, so the first PSCI call landed in corrupted code and the
board hung with the LED stuck.

Reserve the four regions (bl31, optee and two secure SRAM windows; the
addresses come from /proc/iomem of the vendor kernel on this board) and
mark them no-map: the kernel never talks to OP-TEE here, and keeping
firewall-protected RAM in the linear map lets speculative CPU reads raise
sporadic SErrors even though the memory is never allocated.

Co-Authored-By: AI Agent
---
 .../dts/allwinner/sun55i-t527-orangepi-4a.dts | 51 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 51 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-t527-orangepi-4a.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-t527-orangepi-4a.dts
index 0d6318564..10dbd56ed 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-t527-orangepi-4a.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-t527-orangepi-4a.dts
@@ -35,6 +35,57 @@ memory@40000000 {
 		reg = <0x0 0x40000000 0x0 0x80000000>;
 	};
 
+	/*
+	 * The 5.15 BSP reserves this region for BL31 (ARM Trusted Firmware),
+	 * the EL3 secure monitor that serves ALL PSCI calls (SMP core
+	 * bring-up, idle, reset). The mainline DTB reserved nothing and its
+	 * /memory (2GB from 0x40000000) covers 0x48000000 -> the kernel sees those
+	 * 16 MB as free RAM, allocates pages there and OVERWRITES BL31. SMP
+	 * starts before the heartbeat (BL31 still intact) -> 1 beat; right
+	 * after that a PSCI call lands in corrupted code -> hang with the LED
+	 * stuck. Reserving the region (like the BSP does) avoids it. no-map = the
+	 * kernel does not even map it. The vendor U-Boot v2018 does not inject this
+	 * reservation into a foreign DTB, so it has to be static here.
+	 */
+	reserved-memory {
+		#address-cells = <2>;
+		#size-cells = <2>;
+		ranges;
+
+		/*
+		 * The vendor firmware (BL31 + OP-TEE + shared memory) uses SEVERAL
+		 * regions that the vendor U-Boot reserves in the 5.15 FDT but NOT in
+		 * our foreign DTB. Taken from /proc/iomem of the running 5.15. Reserving
+		 * ONLY bl31 let the kernel overwrite OP-TEE/shm -> hang after
+		 * 2 beats. Reserve all 4 (like the BSP).
+		 */
+		/*
+		 * no-map on all four: without it they stay in the linear map and a
+		 * SPECULATIVE CPU read of RAM protected by the
+		 * secure firewall can raise sporadic SErrors even though the
+		 * kernel never allocates them.
+		 */
+		sec-sram1@42350000 {
+			reg = <0x0 0x42350000 0x0 0x00230000>;
+			no-map;
+		};
+
+		sec-sram2@43000000 {
+			reg = <0x0 0x43000000 0x0 0x00094000>;
+			no-map;
+		};
+
+		bl31@48000000 {
+			reg = <0x0 0x48000000 0x0 0x01000000>;
+			no-map;
+		};
+
+		optee@4941d000 {
+			reg = <0x0 0x4941d000 0x0 0x00be3000>;
+			no-map;
+		};
+	};
+
 	/*
 	 * Stub nodes for the vendor U-Boot (v2018.05-t527): its bootm calls
 	 * sunxi_drm_kernel_para_flush(), which looks up /soc/sunxi-drm and /soc/de in the
